add(65,'parent_unspecified','unknown','success_story','floor_play personalization price_value',"Mainly becuase you can access experts in real zooms like they have this courses and classes included that are really good and they would be so expensive if i was purchasing them elsewhere.","Positive commenter values live expert access within Kinedu; identity and purchase are unverified.",date='2026-03-04')
add(66,'parent_unspecified','unknown','desire','floor_play free_alternatives',"Every baby is different of course, but I would love to know what I can generally expect the upcoming weeks/months.","Parent asks for broad expectations while acknowledging individual variation.")
add(67,'parent_unspecified','newborn_0_6_weeks','desire','floor_play personalization',"Is anyone aware of a simple list of activities that parents can/should do with newborns? Ideally  on a week by week basis?","Parent requests a simple weekly activity list.")
add(67,'skeptic','newborn_0_6_weeks','objection','privacy floor_play',"There’s a bunch of apps online and they all seem incredibly spammy and collect a ton of unnecessary data that’s clearly unnecessary .","Parent sees data collection and marketing as costs of using activity apps.")
add(67,'skeptic','newborn_0_6_weeks','desire','floor_play privacy',"It feels like a simple list (or a spreadsheet if you really need to get fancy) should do the trick.","Parent prefers a straightforward artifact to another app.")
add(67,'parent_unspecified','looking_back','success_story','floor_play price_value',"I subscribed to lovevery play kits. They came every few months with information on what to do during each month and how to play with the developmental toys, etc. it’s pricey but I enjoyed it.","Commenter reports purchasing toy kits that bundle guidance with materials.")
add(68,'parent_unspecified','newborn_0_6_weeks','question','floor_play information_overload',"I would love to have some ideas of how best to play with my baby, but has anyone got any experience of these, or any recommendations?","Parent of a twelve-day-old asks whether advertised activity apps are useful.")
add(68,'advisor','unknown','objection','floor_play free_alternatives',"Gently, you don’t need an app for this, especially if it’s paid for.","Commenter directly challenges the need to pay for ordinary baby play ideas.")
add(68,'parent_unspecified','unknown','belief','personalization price_value',"Nara has a simple interface and only shows you what you want.","Commenter describes selective display as valuable; app pricing claims need separate current verification.")
add(70,'parent_unspecified','unknown','objection','floor_play price_value',"I have 3 apps but their free version seems lacking almost intentionally.","Parent compares paid activity-app tiers in a 2020 thread.")
add(70,'parent_unspecified','unknown','success_story','floor_play personalization',"You get daily activities, and you can see the whole plan for the week.","Kinedu commenter values an overview; the same reply offers a referral code.")
add(70,'reviewer','unknown','objection','subscription_fatigue price_value',"They then charged me the full year subscription price immediately. There was no free trial period.","A 2025 commenter alleges a billing issue; not independently verified or proof of current practice.",date='2025-11-12')
add(71,'parent_unspecified','newborn_0_6_weeks','question','floor_play price_value',"I have a 6 week old baby and wondering if anyone here used Kinedu and if Its worth It?","Parent asks whether a paid activity app would be useful.")
add(71,'parent_unspecified','looking_back','belief','floor_play personalization',"I don’t use it as much anymore now that my LO is getting older, but it definitely helped give me more ideas on things to do with my daughter.","Commenter reports a useful early stage followed by less use; reply offers a referral code.")
add(71,'parent_unspecified','unknown','success_story','floor_play personalization',"They will give you your own personalized plan based on where your child is developmentally, or you can pick activities yourself from their catalog.","Commenter describes ability-based recommendations and self-selected alternatives in 2021.")

add(73,'parent_unspecified','return_to_work','question','pumping_schedule return_to_work',"I have a meeting with my boss on Monday to go over what my new responsibilities will be since I’m in a new role at work and I need to mention that I will need to pump while I’m there. How do I come up with a schedule for pumping…?","Parent needs a concrete proposal before a meeting with their manager.")
add(74,'partner','return_to_work','question','pumping_schedule return_to_work',"She would love to continue breastfeeding/ pumping when she can but we're not sure how to handle the transition or if it'll even be possible.","Partner of a nurse working twelve-hour nights asks about feasible feeding options.")
add(74,'gave_up_parent','return_to_work','failure_story','pumping_schedule return_to_work',"I had planned to continue pumping back at work as a teacher and I lasted a week before starting the weaning process.","Teacher reports abandoning an intended pumping routine.")
add(74,'gave_up_parent','return_to_work','objection','pumping_schedule not_enough_time',"It felt impossible with my schedule and I was spending the little free time I had pumping instead of getting work done and was falling behind on my job.","Teacher describes the cost to preparation time rather than lack of scheduling information.")
add(76,'parent_unspecified','return_to_work','belief','pumping_schedule return_to_work',"When I return to work, I'll be doing three, 12 hour shifts. Thankfully they are great about supporting me with pumping and have a lactation room I can use as well.","Parent seeks planning despite an explicitly supportive workplace.")
add(76,'parent_unspecified','return_to_work','question','pumping_schedule personalization',"On my days home from work, can I go back to pumping every 3 hours or should I remain consistent and just stay at every 4 hours once I transition to that?","Parent asks about workday versus non-workday consistency; individualized lactation review is outside a logistics-only report.")
add(78,'advisor','return_to_work','others_said','pumping_schedule return_to_work',"I have accommodated many pumping mothers schedules and forced their planning time to be when they needed to pump. Talk to your admin!","Self-described assistant principal says school scheduling requires administrative involvement.")
add(78,'parent_unspecified','return_to_work','question','pumping_schedule not_enough_time',"If I pump during lunch and my plan time when do I collaborate and/ or make copies?","Elementary teacher explains that available break slots also contain essential job tasks.",date='2025-03-17')
add(78,'parent_unspecified','return_to_work','success_story','pumping_schedule household_support',"My coworker will make copies if I need them.  My admin was extremely supportive thankfully!","Teacher reports that coworker coverage helped make a plan workable.",date='2025-03-17')
add(80,'parent_unspecified','pregnancy_late','desire','pumping_schedule birth_preparation',"I am a teacher, so I need to communicate with my principal what times before they can create a master schedule / figure out coverage for me.","Expecting teacher needs early coordination with school timetabling and staff coverage.")
add(81,'parent_unspecified','return_to_work','pain','pumping_schedule personalization',"It’ll be 12 hour shifts, three days a week. Three weeks I’ll be on days 7a-7p, then I’ll switch to nights 7p-7a for three weeks.","Parent has rotating shift blocks rather than one fixed daily schedule.")
add(81,'parent_unspecified','return_to_work','desire','pumping_schedule personalization',"Just looking for any tips or advice for people that have similar schedules.","Parent wants examples that match their work pattern.")
add(83,'parent_unspecified','return_to_work','trigger_moment','pumping_schedule return_to_work',"Today is my last day of maternity leave. I go back to work tomorrow. I'm a nurse who works 12 hour shifts and also have a 30 minute drive to and from the hospital.","Nurse seeks a practical plan on the final day before returning.")
add(83,'parent_unspecified','return_to_work','success_story','pumping_schedule free_alternatives personalization',"Chat GPT was super helpful to me to put together a pumping schedule. You can just give it your commute time, shift time,  if there are any times during your shift that you'd prefer pumping, and how many pumps you need. You can then revise from there.","Commenter reports using general-purpose AI for the same scheduling artifact a paid report might offer.")

add(84,'experienced_mother','looking_back','regret','household_support second_baby partner_mental_load',"I thought husband takes care of toddler, I take care of baby. I forgot— who takes care of ME?!","Commenter describes a missing responsibility in a two-child postpartum plan.")
add(84,'parent_unspecified','pregnancy_late','question','household_support second_baby daycare_handoff',"Will she keep going to daycare? How will she get there (daycare is 30 minutes each way from home, so her going means 2 hours of driving daily)?","Expecting second-time parent names concrete transport decisions that generic advice misses.")
add(84,'parent_unspecified','unknown','objection','household_support personalization',"Lots of us dont have the option of consistent help, and even if our spouse is willing they might not be able","Commenter says willingness and practical capacity are different constraints.",date='2025-10-02')
add(85,'parent_unspecified','looking_back','success_story','household_support birth_preparation',"A postpartum plan - we sat down two weeks before my ceaser and spoke about what life postpartum would look like while my husband was home with me.","Commenter reports discussing a practical plan before delivery.",date='')
add(85,'parent_unspecified','looking_back','belief','household_support personalization',"examples of “quick breaks” we could take each (eg. Short shower, walk the dog, cup of tea outside)","Their plan included small restorative breaks rather than only baby-care tasks.",date='')
add(88,'advisor','unknown','advice_given','household_support personalization',"Its going to take a few weeks to settle into a routine that works and as soon as you do baby will grow and change and you will have to change again.","Commenter argues for a revisable plan; timing is the commenter's view, not an established estimate.",date='')
add(88,'parent_unspecified','pregnancy_late','belief','household_support partner_mental_load',"This works for us because my spouse is interested in being helpful and realistic about postpartum recovery.","Expecting second-time parent identifies partner cooperation as an enabling condition.")
add(89,'parent_unspecified','pregnancy_late','desire','household_support birth_preparation',"He’s taking the first four weeks off to be with me and the baby so would like to establish something now to have a general idea.","Expecting parent wants a plan adapted to the partner's leave.")
add(89,'parent_unspecified','pregnancy_late','belief','household_support personalization',"We also have two Siberian husky furbabies to factor into the equation (he does the walks; one morning and one evening, totalling to 2 hours a day)","Pet care is a material constraint in this household's plan.")
add(89,'parent_unspecified','newborn_0_6_weeks','desire','household_support return_to_work',"I am not sure what we will do when he goes back to work.","Commenter has a working leave-period arrangement but no plan for the return transition.",date='2025-01-22')
add(89,'parent_unspecified','newborn_0_6_weeks','success_story','household_support personalization',"We have a little debrief every morning to talk about how the night went and what we learned and want to try again the following night.","Commenter describes revising household arrangements after each night.",date='2025-01-22')
add(90,'parent_unspecified','looking_back','success_story','household_support meal_planning',"He did all the other house upkeep, though we both agreed that folding laundry was not a priority and lived out of baskets.","Commenter describes an explicit lower-priority chore agreement.",date='2022-06-26')
add(90,'expecting_mother','pregnancy_late','question','household_support pumping_schedule',"Can you explain to me how 6-7 sleep shifts work if I have to pump or breastfeed? I’m a ftm due in January and I hear this a lot and don’t know how it works.","Expecting mother wants a plan that accounts for feeding realities rather than repeating sleep-shift advice.",date='2022-06-26')
add(91,'parent_unspecified','pregnancy_late','others_said','household_support conflicting_advice',"Two of my friends are new moms (4 months and 2 months) and keep telling me it’ll NEVER happen.","Expecting parent receives discouraging reactions to a proposed postpartum sleep arrangement.")
add(91,'parent_unspecified','pregnancy_late','desire','household_support personalization',"Posting my plan here and genuinely curious if you think a plan like this is impossible, like my friends are loving telling me, or if you think it’s reasonable.","Parent asks strangers to review the feasibility of a specific plan.")
add(91,'parent_unspecified','baby_6_16_weeks','success_story','household_support personalization',"I will disagree with most of the comments and say that a version of this worked great for my husband and I!","Commenter reports a different experience; not a guaranteed infant or parent sleep outcome.")
add(92,'new_mother','looking_back','belief','birth_preparation free_alternatives',"My LO made her grand entrance 6 weeks ago so I wanted to share the checklist I used to get ready for her.","First-time mother shares a free preparation checklist.")
add(92,'new_mother','looking_back','belief','birth_preparation personalization',"Quick note: some items are US specific and might not apply if you are in another country.","Author explicitly identifies geographic limits of a generic checklist.")

